                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "🎮 Elendia Ceus Review ⭐⭐⭐☆☆ (3/5)\n\nThe Good: 📖 The story itself is interesting and keeps you engaged throughout the game.\n\n💰 Fair price when on sale, around €1. Worth it at that cost.\n\nThe Bad: ⚔️ Unbalanced Battles – This is the biggest issue. Some fights are extremely easy, while others are way too difficult. I could only finish the game using Cheat Engine. Without cheats, it simply wasn't possible for me.\n\n👙 Skimpy Clothing – Female characters wear unnecessarily revealing outfits. I don't believe this is needed to make a good game. It feels gratuitous.\n\n❓ Confusing Ending – After all the credits, there's a scene where a woman delivers a baby named Teresa in a hospital. I still don't get what this had to do with the game or the story.\n\nVerdict: The story saves this game, but the battle balance and questionable design choices drag it down. If you grab it on sale for around €1, you might find it worth the risk. At full price? Probably skip it.\n\nRecommendation: Wait for a sale and come prepared with a difficulty mod or cheat tool if needed.",
